---
const principles=[{title:'Identity is independent of applications',body:'An application can interact with a Relay identity without becoming the identity itself.'},{title:'Records are portable',body:"Digital information has protocol-level identity and structure, rather than existing only as an application's internal object."},{title:'Relationships outlast any one application',body:'Connections between identities do not need to disappear because a particular application is abandoned.'},{title:'Applications are participants, not owners',body:"Applications interact with a person's digital presence according to defined permissions and capabilities, rather than inherently controlling it."},{title:'Infrastructure is replaceable',body:"Changing repository or infrastructure providers shouldn't require a person's digital identity and presence to begin again."}];
---
<section id="principles"><div class="prose-wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="kicker">Principles</span><h2>What Relay is built on</h2></div><ul class="principle-list">{principles.map((p)=><li><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.body}</p></li>)}</ul></div></section>
<style>.principle-list{list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.75rem}.principle-list li{padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.principle-list li:first-child{padding-top:0;border-top:none}.principle-list h3{margin-bottom:.5rem}</style>
